# Close-pass mirror cadence. systemd calendars have no ET, so the window is
# expressed as the UTC SPAN that covers the evening publish window in BOTH DST
# regimes and the pass itself no-ops when there is nothing new:
#   EDT  16:15 ET = 20:15Z   ...   18:30 ET = 22:30Z
#   EST  16:15 ET = 21:15Z   ...   18:30 ET = 23:30Z
# so 20..23 UTC covers both ends. One schedule, one window, no second copy of
# "when does the evening board land" — the pass's own dedup (served as_of ==
# fetched as_of) is what turns ~40 ticks into exactly one write a day, so the
# span can be generous without the artifact being rewritten on every tick.
#
# The span deliberately runs PAST the 18:30 ET SLA rather than stopping at it: a
# board that publishes late must still reach the page, and the sentinel's
# first-fresh-at record is what says it was late. Stopping the mirror at the
# deadline would turn a late board into a missing one.
#
# :02/5 rather than :00/5 — the mac pass publishes to R2 on no fixed second, and
# two minutes of offset keeps this lane off the top-of-minute contention every
# other timer on the box shares. Publication is an atomic rename either way, so
# a read is never partial.
[Unit]
Description=Mirror the close-pass provisional board across the evening window

[Timer]
OnCalendar=Mon..Fri *-*-* 20..23:02/5:00 UTC
AccuracySec=1s
RandomizedDelaySec=10s
Persistent=false
Unit=macro-live-closepass.service

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
